module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.PopescuLiftPresentation

@[expose] public section

universe a c

namespace Algebra

/-- The explicit prepared quotient becomes smooth after inverting the base element.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 07CP, key equality and proof of property (b).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-lift-smooth-away).

Proof: Write P = R[x], Q = R[x,z], u_j = f_j - π z_j, and
p_{kl} = a_k z_l - Σ_{j ∈ E_k} h_{klj} z_j - π g_{kl}. The Prepared relation
implies π p_{kl} = -a_k u_l + Σ_{j ∈ E_k} h_{klj} u_j in Q.
After inverting π, every p_{kl} belongs to the ideal generated by the u_j.
Thus the localized defining ideal is generated just by the u_j. Substitution
z_j = π⁻¹ f_j gives an R-algebra isomorphism from its quotient to P[1/π]:
the inverse sends each original variable to its quotient class. The u_j vanish
under substitution, and the relation above makes all the p_{kl} vanish as well;
on the other composite, u_j = 0 and invertibility of π recover each z_j.
The polynomial algebra P is smooth over R, and principal localization is smooth
and preserves smoothness by composition. Transfer this smoothness across the
isomorphism. Finally the ULift algebra equivalence identifies the localization
of the quotient with the displayed localization of d.liftingAlgebra.
This argument uses only the cleared relations, and needs neither the annihilator
hypothesis nor the maps on the special fibre.
-/
theorem popescu_lift_smooth_away (R : Type a) (Cbar : Type c)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing Cbar] [Algebra R Cbar] (π : R)
    [Algebra (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 2} : Set R)) Cbar]
    (d : PopescuLiftPresentation R Cbar π) (hd : d.Prepared) :
    Smooth R (Localization.Away (algebraMap R d.liftingAlgebra π)) := by sorry

end Algebra
